# No secrets in code

If you see a secret in repo files — even if Aziz pasted it by hand — **stop and warn in the first sentence**. Do not leave it. Do not commit it. Move it to `/root/carland.env` (server) or a gitignored local env.

JWT/HMAC, DB/mail/SMS passwords, API keys (Brevo, MSM, LSIM, SIMA, IDDA, Hyper, Kong), `CARLAND_INTERNAL_TOKEN`, admin PIN, partner webhook secrets, Firebase JSON, Postman HMAC/Identifier must not live in git.

OK in git: public URLs, `${ENV_VAR}`, empty `.env.example`.

If hardcoded: tell him **bu secret git'e giremez**, replace with `${...}` / `@Value`, put the value only in `/root/carland.env`, do not echo the secret in chat.
